<p>If you have followed me for any time, you will know I have been an <a href="https://joshblais.com/blog/Use-Emacs">avid emacs user since 2020</a>.
But, in simplifying things, I am going away from it for a few reasons - I find it slow, it does too much, and I want to replicate my dev environment everywhere with low latancy.
Emacs is great but I feel as if Neovim is the future and I want to skate to where the puck is going (to show my Canadian side).
It is apparent to me that emacs has its time and place, but with the rapid movement of Neovim, I see it as <strong>the</strong> place to be.
We will configure this with all plugins and necessary additions that I use, and will be building from NVChad’s base config - which is <em>really good</em> and has such sane defaults.</p>
